{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Preserve the existing contents of /srv/inventory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The same two existing files remain present with unchanged sizes and SHA-256 hashes from the preparation baseline through the repair and post-restart verification.","evidence_ids":["prepared-inventory-data","cmd-a37e91ec4c4c4689","cmd-917cee2035cc4a6e","cmd-a47da3c36f0b482a"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Make the existing inventory data owned by inventorysvc.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The inventorysvc account was established and every observed directory and file under /srv/inventory is owned by inventorysvc, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-94208ca03fb54918","cmd-917cee2035cc4a6e","cmd-a47da3c36f0b482a"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Make the inventory data readable by inventory-readers.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All observed inventory paths have group inventory-readers, directories provide group traversal, files provide group read permission, and direct reads using that group succeeded before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-94208ca03fb54918","cmd-917cee2035cc4a6e","cmd-a47da3c36f0b482a"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Make /srv/inventory inaccessible to other users.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Directories have mode 0750 and files mode 0640, leaving no permissions for the POSIX other class. Direct unrelated-user read and traversal tests were denied before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-917cee2035cc4a6e","cmd-a47da3c36f0b482a"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"All observed mutations had clear roles: account/group creation and ownership/mode changes implemented the repair, while the reboot and its temporary log supported the mandatory restart protocol. No unnecessary mutation was identified. The two interrupted probes were read-only checks during reboot. Post-executor observations show no failed services, healthy package state, or unexplained exposure; temporary-file and socket differences are normal reboot effects.","evidence_ids":["cmd-94208ca03fb54918","cmd-0860a8280e1744eb","cmd-b5d3cc29a97e49f3","cmd-7e03df0258fe4f43","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct metadata, content-hash, and effective-access evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 was running before restart, acknowledged the restart, returned with a different boot identity, and retained the identities, permissions, access behavior, and data. The fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["getfacl was unavailable, so named ACLs were not enumerated directly; however, restrictive mode bits and successful unrelated-user denial tests provide strong direct evidence of the required access behavior.","The topology contains no cluster service, so restart recovery evidence appropriately covers node health, identities, filesystem data, and permissions rather than cluster state."]}
